# Official interface references

Current consumer documentation successor (2026-11-09): the installation README
is shared-toolbox/README.md under the dev_audit workspace. Consult
shared-toolbox/docs/consumer-integration.md for exec/discovery/mounts/results and
shared-toolbox/docs/application.md for operator preparation, volumes and SELinux.
Module documentation is in shared-toolbox/tools/<tool>/README.md; it is not a
consumer executable path. native-execution.md is now a compatibility pointer.
Ox setup and explicit SELinux selection are documented in scripts/README.md.
The dated observations below retain their historical version/activation scope.

These are upstream sources consulted for the adapter interfaces, not claims of
local scanner execution. The versioned references below preserve the interface
research history; they do not select the active central version. Current transport,
prerequisites and limitations are in scripts/README.md. Root erase.md is a
preserved historical note, not an operational preparation guide.

- Gitleaks: [8.30.1](https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks/releases/tag/v8.30.1); check `gitleaks / history`.
- OSV Scanner: [2.7.0](https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/releases/tag/v2.7.0); check `osv`.
- Opengrep: [1.33.1](https://github.com/opengrep/opengrep/releases/tag/v1.33.1); check `opengrep`.
- cargo-audit: [0.22.2](https://github.com/RustSec/rustsec/releases/tag/cargo-audit/v0.22.2); check `audit`.
- cargo-deny: [0.20.2](https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-deny/releases/tag/0.20.2); check `deny`.
- cargo-machete: [0.9.2](https://github.com/bnjbvr/cargo-machete/releases/tag/v0.9.2); check `machete`.
- Ruff: [0.17.4](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/releases/tag/0.17.4); check `ruff`.
- Bandit: [1.9.4](https://github.com/PyCQA/bandit/releases/tag/1.9.4); check `bandit`.
- cargo-llvm-cov: [0.9.1](https://github.com/taiki-e/cargo-llvm-cov/releases/tag/v0.9.1); check `coverage (complementar)`.
- cargo-geiger: [0.13.0](https://github.com/geiger-rs/cargo-geiger/releases/tag/cargo-geiger-0.13.0); check `geiger (complementar)`.
- Trivy: [0.76.2](https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/releases/tag/v0.76.2); check `trivy (complementar)`.
- Syft: [1.57.0](https://github.com/anchore/syft/releases/tag/v1.57.0); check `sbom (complementar)`.
- Grype: [0.121.2](https://github.com/anchore/grype/releases/tag/v0.121.2); check `grype (complementar)`.
- YARA-X: [1.23.0](https://github.com/VirusTotal/yara-x/releases/tag/v1.23.0); check `malware (complementar)`.
- ShellCheck: [0.11.0](https://github.com/koalaman/shellcheck/releases/tag/v0.11.0); check `shellcheck (complementar)`.

Offline OSV: https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/blob/main/docs/offline-mode.md
Offline cargo-deny: https://embarkstudios.github.io/cargo-deny/cli/common.html
RustSec no-fetch/no-yanked: https://github.com/RustSec/rustsec/blob/main/cargo-audit/src/commands/audit.rs
Opengrep local rule interface: https://github.com/opengrep/opengrep
Trivy air-gap: https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/advanced/air-gap/
YARA JSON schema: https://github.com/VirusTotal/yara-x/blob/main/cli/src/commands/scan.rs
Qodana linter matrix: https://www.jetbrains.com/help/qodana/linters.html

No unofficial Rust Qodana image or foreign-stack rules are required. Tool and
database licensing/compatibility require review before preparation/distribution.

Geiger virtual-manifest rejection and member report schema:
https://github.com/geiger-rs/cargo-geiger/blob/master/cargo-geiger/src/main.rs
https://github.com/geiger-rs/cargo-geiger/blob/master/cargo-geiger-serde/src/report.rs

## Configuration review — 2026-11-06

Current official documentation consulted for scripts-toolchain-config (not a
statement that every native scanner is installed or its scan completed):

| Solution | Official contract | Ox use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Ruff | [configuration](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/configuration/), [0.11.13 schema](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/astral-sh/ruff/0.11.13/ruff.schema.json) | Python 3.11, correctness/security/bug rules, no fixes or noqa suppression in native mode |
| Bandit | [configuration](https://bandit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/config.html) | Explicit YAML and INI, all plugins, no nosec or baseline |
| Gitleaks | [upstream CLI](https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks) | Default detector rules, redacted reports; native inline allows disabled |
| ShellCheck | [directives and rcfile](https://github.com/koalaman/shellcheck/wiki/Directive) | Local source resolution, no global disabled diagnostics |
| OSV | [configuration at 2.0.2](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/osv-scanner/v2.0.2/docs/configuration.md), [offline mode](https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/usage/offline-mode/) | Explicit empty exclusion lists, reviewed offline database |
| Opengrep | [upstream](https://github.com/opengrep/opengrep) | Local Rust/Python rules, strict parsing, no inline suppression/metrics |
| RustSec | [config](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rustsec/rustsec/main/cargo-audit/src/config.rs), [example](https://github.com/rustsec/rustsec/blob/main/cargo-audit/audit.toml.example) | Private cwd config takes precedence; no fetch/yank index, informational warnings fail |
| cargo-deny | [config](https://embarkstudios.github.io/cargo-deny/checks/cfg.html), [licenses](https://embarkstudios.github.io/cargo-deny/checks/licenses/cfg.html), [sources](https://embarkstudios.github.io/cargo-deny/checks/sources/cfg.html) | Linux target, unknown registry/Git rejected, no license grants, duplicates/wildcards fail |
| Machete | [JSON and metadata](https://github.com/bnjbvr/cargo-machete#json-output) | Global binary, no fix/metadata dependency resolution; upstream clean JSON can be `{}` |
| llvm-cov | [CLI and environment](https://github.com/taiki-e/cargo-llvm-cov) | Isolated output, existing LLVM component, no automatic setup or fabricated coverage threshold |
| Geiger | [upstream](https://github.com/geiger-rs/cargo-geiger), [CLI](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/geiger-rs/cargo-geiger/master/cargo-geiger/src/cli.rs) | Each member manifest; unsafe inventory, not a safety verdict |
| Trivy | [configuration](https://trivy.dev/docs/latest/references/configuration/config-file/) | Explicit offline DB and empty ignore file; all severities/unfixed vulnerabilities |
| Syft | [configuration](https://oss.anchore.com/docs/reference/syft/configuration/) | No update check; inventory only |
| Grype | [0.119.0 configuration](https://oss.anchore.com/docs/reference/grype/configuration/) | Updates disabled; age validation, no ignore rules/fix-state filtering |
| YARA-X | [CLI](https://virustotal.github.io/yara-x/docs/cli/commands/) | Local indicator rules and structured scan output; no artificial config file for CLI-only options |

The local guide `.local/usage.md` and shared-toolbox source were also inspected.
Historical catalog versions differed from the native references above: the removed toolbox.json pinned the
actual candidate catalog, not an assumed latest version. Ruff/Gitleaks/ShellCheck
and Grype have candidate adapters; all other scanner adapters in that toolbox
are research-blocked. Playwright is inapplicable to this native Iced product.
No Dockerfile, lock or successful schema validation establishes execution.

## Preparation and real CLI verification — 2026-11-06

OSV 2.7.0's documented offline layout differs from the SCALIBR matcher it uses:
[matcher at the pinned dependency](https://github.com/google/osv-scalibr/blob/5be78a00e3c2/enricher/vulnmatch/osvlocal/matcher.go).
The adapter sets both cache variables and preparation preserves both layouts.
[OSV source licenses](https://google.github.io/osv.dev/data/) and
[RustSec advisory licenses](https://docs.rs/rustsec/latest/rustsec/advisory/enum.License.html)
are distinct from scanner licenses. The current RustSec snapshot retains CC0 and
CC-BY metadata/attributions. [Grype database CLI](https://oss.anchore.com/docs/reference/grype/cli/)
and [Trivy DB](https://trivy.dev/docs/dev/docs/configuration/db/) guide optional preparation.
Opengrep 1.33.1 help and real probes established its current flag/parser contract;
local rules revision 2 import no external rules.

## Historical Toolbox ownership contract inspected — 2026-11-07

Current integration uses the installed shared-toolbox sources, inspected read-only:
`docs/configuration.md`, `toolbox/config.py`, `toolbox/databases.py`,
`toolbox/runner.py`, Trivy 0.76.2 and OSV 2.7.0 versioned adapters and Grype adapter.
The real `examples/offline-security/toolbox.images.lock.json` supplies exact image
and snapshot records. No latest-version claim or Docker change is made. Earlier
native preparation observations above remain historical.


## Native exec successor — 2026-11-08

Versioned official sources inspected for the candidate interfaces (no central
version is active; these are not evidence of scanner operation):
- [Gitleaks 8.24.3 flags](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gitleaks/gitleaks/v8.24.3/cmd/root.go).
- [Ruff 0.11.13 arguments](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/astral-sh/ruff/0.11.13/crates/ruff/src/args.rs).
- [Bandit 1.8.3 CLI/INI](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PyCQA/bandit/1.8.3/bandit/cli/main.py).
- [ShellCheck 0.11.0 formats and exits](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/koalaman/shellcheck/v0.11.0/shellcheck.hs).
- [Grype 0.119.0 age policy](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/anchore/grype/v0.119.0/cmd/grype/cli/options/database.go).

Other native flags/parsers are retained from the existing Ox integration; their
compatibility with the centrally activated version needs actual qualification.
YARA-X 1.0.0 versioned source lookup failed; no compatibility approval is claimed.
The public native contract, consumer integration, operations, native-validation
and current README/doc.md sections were read from shared-toolbox. They supersede
consumer locks, adapters and fixed DB snapshots as exec prerequisites.
